    "essay": "Naukri's September JobSpeak report shows overall white-collar hiring rose just 1% year-on-year, while artificial intelligence and machine learning roles jumped 20%. The gap points to employers concentrating demand in specialized skills rather than expanding headcount broadly. Global capability centre hiring grew 4% overall, but within BPO and IT-enabled services, GCC hiring jumped 59%. Auto hiring rose 11%, led by Hyderabad, Chennai and Bengaluru. Banking and financial services stayed stable but saw a 14% increase in fresher hiring. IT and software services declined 4% despite the AI/ML surge, showing the growth is narrow. For Info Edge, this mix supports premium listings in AI and GCC roles but caps the broader recruiter base.",
